  "fixes_applied_on_linux": [
    "route_manager stored its action goal handle in self.handle, which collides with the read-only rclpy Node.handle property; renamed to goal_handle.",
    "bev_node transformed the map-frame local goal at the scan stamp while AMCL's map->odom trailed by a few milliseconds; the goal now uses the latest TF, removing periodic dropped observations.",
    "PathTracker could deadlock after stopping with the mapped footprint touching an obstacle (AMCL drift): every visibility chord failed. It now retries with the bare radius and, when the footprint is still inside the minimum guard, follows a short 0.4 m carrot on the planner's path, resuming visible lookahead once a chord is clear."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "These are ROS/Gazebo results on the open home map, not the Windows 2D holdout. The v1 and v2 weights behave almost identically on the tested home-map goals; the published v2 gain is the 96-episode 2D holdout with visible carrots and the v2 safety/stuck semantics.",
    "Only two final goals plus one reset sequence were measured here; this is not a success-rate estimate.",
    "Repeated Gazebo launches occasionally leave Nav2 lifecycle nodes stuck in 'unconfigured' when old nodes are still shutting down; a clean restart resolves it."
  ]
